{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Take me back to the [C]carolinas
I long to [G]see my mountain [C]home
[F]Take me back to the [C]carolinas
Where I can [G]rest no more to [C]roam
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I ran around the blue ridge mountains
Met the prettiest girl I’d ever seen
Spend our nights in swaying pine trees
I wanna go back back to the mountain cool
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
I left her there in a little cabin
Promised her I’d see her soon
I’ll be home before the harvest
When the dogwoods begin to bloom
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_chorus}
I rambled round and lost her memory
Went out west and forgot her name
When I see those rocky mountains
I long to be back home again
{end_of_chorus}
